resolution: "Updated pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog to 2026.7.10, TypeScript to 7.0.2, Node types to 26.1.1, checkout to v7, aligned runtime minimums, stopped tracking generated dist, made changelog generation history-safe, and reconciled stale duplicate/completed pm items."
expected_result: "Warning-free current extension with complete native Linear registrations, deterministic daily release gates, clean package artifacts, validated project history, and no sensitive tracked data."
actual_result: 51 tests and full release gate pass; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; package tarball contains built dist; isolated installed doctor reports zero warnings with commands/importers/exporter/schema/preflight; credential-free validate and fake-key offline state+cycle dry-run behave correctly; secret scans found no matches.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-10T11:10:40.558Z",codex,"PR #22 independent verification (2026-07-10): npm ci/build passed; full Node suite 51/51 passed after regression fix 1665b5a. Throwaway install + pm --help hang check passed. --cycle dry-runs for linear sync/import emitted server-side containsIgnoreCase filter and cycle=\"Sprint 7\"; surrounding whitespace normalized; missing value exited 2 cleanly. Mocked in-process HTTP 401/403 with fake key (no real Linear API traffic) exited 2 immediately with actionable LINEAR_API_KEY guidance. Default no-cycle dry-run output matched origin/main byte-for-byte (1634 bytes). Six bot threads handled (4 valid +1/addressed, 2 obsolete-parser -1/not applicable). Re-review requested after push."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T01:02:04.293Z",codex,"When a public repository has rewritten history, full --all-release-tags regeneration cannot reconstruct non-ancestor releases; use the same since-previous-tag prepend window for generation, validation, and release notes."
